<title>Capelli Sport — CS Certification Exam · Set 6</title>
<!--[if gte mso 9]><xml><w:WordDocument><w:View>Print</w:View><w:Zoom>100</w:Zoom></w:WordDocument></xml><![endif]-->
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #1a1a2e; line-height: 1.4; }
h1 { font-size: 20pt; color: #0b2e6b; border-bottom: 2px solid #0b2e6b; padding-bottom: 4pt; }
h2 { font-size: 15pt; color: #0b2e6b; margin-top: 16pt; }
h3 { font-size: 12.5pt; color: #14213d; margin-top: 12pt; }
hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #b0b8c4; }
strong { color: #0b2e6b; }
blockquote { background: #eef2f7; border-left: 3pt solid #0b2e6b; margin: 8pt 0; padding: 6pt 12pt; font-style: italic; }
ul, ol { margin: 6pt 0 6pt 12pt; }
li { margin: 3pt 0; }
code { font-family: Consolas, monospace; background: #eef2f7; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; margin: 10pt 0; font-size: 10.5pt; }
th { background: #0b2e6b; color: #ffffff; }
th, td { border: 1px solid #9aa5b4; padding: 4pt 8pt; text-align: left; }
</style></head>
<body><h1>Capelli Sport — CS Certification Exam · Set 6</h1>
<p><strong>Name: ____________________   Date: __________   Score: ______ / 100</strong></p>
<p>Closed book. Answer in the voice of the agent handling the ticket. For each scenario, state <strong>how you handle it</strong> (route + action) and <strong>the one trap</strong> that would fail the ticket. <strong>Section A — 6 points each; Section B (multiple choice) — 2 points each. Total 100.</strong></p>
<hr>
<p><strong>Q1.</strong> <em>"Your email says my order shipped and gave me a UPS number, but when I click it there's no information at all. Has it really shipped?"</em> How do you reassure the customer?</p>
<p><strong>Q2.</strong> <em>"If you can't get my order here faster, then refund me the shipping I paid — I shouldn't pay for shipping on something this late."</em> How do you handle this (rush + shipping-refund) request?</p>
<p><strong>Q3.</strong> <em>"We bought my son a Capelli backpack and it's already ripping at the seam after a couple of months. He needs it to last the season."</em> How do you handle an equipment/bag defect?</p>
<p><strong>Q4.</strong> <em>"Before I ship my return back — will you refund what I paid for shipping too?"</em> What do you tell the customer?</p>
<p><strong>Q5.</strong> <em>"My order is way past the time you promised. I get that things happen, but at minimum please refund the shipping cost."</em> How do you handle the goodwill shipping refund?</p>
<p><strong>Q6.</strong> <em>"I checked out as a guest and now I can't see my order or order individual items. What do I do?"</em> Walk through the fix.</p>
<p><strong>Q7.</strong> <em>"My son's number changed this season, but the ordering site still shows his old number and won't let me change it before paying."</em> How do you handle this?</p>
<p><strong>Q8.</strong> <em>"The size Large I want is out of stock. I'm not picky about color — is there anything you can do?"</em> What can you offer?</p>
<p><strong>Q9. Spot the mistake.</strong> A teammate drafted this reply — identify <strong>every</strong> thing wrong with it:</p>
<blockquote><em>"Hi — I've emailed GT and RI in planning to check OBD status on your order. Once the wave releases I'll let you know. Please don't reply in the meantime."</em></blockquote>
<p>List each error and give the corrected customer-facing message.</p>
<p><strong>Q10. Missing item, wants refund.</strong> <em>"I only got 4 of the 5 things I ordered — the white hat wasn't in the box. Honestly I've waited long enough, I'd rather just get refunded for it."</em> How do you handle a missing item where the customer now prefers a refund?</p>
<hr>
<h2>Section B — Multiple Choice (Q11–Q30)</h2>
<p>Choose the single best answer. 2 points each.</p>
<p><strong>11.</strong> UPS tracking shows "no information" right after shipping because:</p>
<ul><li>A) It's lost</li><li>B) UPS hasn't scanned it yet; movement shows after the scan</li><li>C) The number is wrong</li><li>D) It was cancelled</li></ul>
<p><strong>12.</strong> "Refund my shipping because it's late" is:</p>
<ul><li>A) A goodwill gesture needing internal approval</li><li>B) Automatic</li><li>C) Never possible</li><li>D) The club's call</li></ul>
<p><strong>13.</strong> A bag ripping at the seam is:</p>
<ul><li>A) Wear and tear, no action</li><li>B) The customer's fault</li><li>C) A defect — photo + replacement (may need DM approval)</li><li>D) A standard return</li></ul>
<p><strong>14.</strong> Return shipping cost is:</p>
<ul><li>A) Refunded</li><li>B) Not refunded</li><li>C) Store credit</li><li>D) Half refunded</li></ul>
<p><strong>15.</strong> A guest-checkout customer wants individual items. First:</p>
<ul><li>A) Create an account (same email) and link the order</li><li>B) Reorder</li><li>C) Call</li><li>D) Nothing</li></ul>
<p><strong>16.</strong> A player's number shows the old value on the site. You:</p>
<ul><li>A) Change it yourself</li><li>B) Tell them the club must update the roster</li><li>C) Refund</li><li>D) Cancel</li></ul>
<p><strong>17.</strong> OOS but the customer is flexible on color:</p>
<ul><li>A) Cancel</li><li>B) Refund only</li><li>C) Offer the same item/size in an alternative color (if available)</li><li>D) Ship anything</li></ul>
<p><strong>18.</strong> Which is an internal fulfillment term (never to customers)?</p>
<ul><li>A) UPS</li><li>B) OBD</li><li>C) Tracking</li><li>D) Return policy</li></ul>
<p><strong>19.</strong> A missing item where the customer now prefers a refund:</p>
<ul><li>A) Confirm it's missing, then refund that item</li><li>B) Reship anyway</li><li>C) Ignore</li><li>D) Escalate to the club</li></ul>
<p><strong>20.</strong> In-stock item shipping timeline (after processing):</p>
<ul><li>A) 1–3 business days</li><li>B) 5 weeks</li><li>C) 3–6 weeks</li><li>D) Same day</li></ul>
<p><strong>21.</strong> Which must NEVER appear in a customer email?</p>
<ul><li>A) A UPS link</li><li>B) A "PLS DO NOT RESPOND" internal note</li><li>C) The order number</li><li>D) The return address</li></ul>
<p><strong>22.</strong> Mandatory-kit items in the cart must:</p>
<ul><li>A) Be removed to check out</li><li>B) Stay in the cart (removing a required item breaks checkout)</li><li>C) Be reordered</li><li>D) Be split</li></ul>
<p><strong>23.</strong> A defective-item replacement is shipped in:</p>
<ul><li>A) The same size/form</li><li>B) A bigger size</li><li>C) Any size</li><li>D) The customer's choice</li></ul>
<p><strong>24.</strong> A refund on the statement shows as:</p>
<ul><li>A) The club</li><li>B) "CAPELLI SPORT"</li><li>C) "REFUND"</li><li>D) The bank name</li></ul>
<p><strong>25.</strong> Expedited shipping is offered:</p>
<ul><li>A) For a fee</li><li>B) Never</li><li>C) For tournaments</li><li>D) On Shopify</li></ul>
<p><strong>26.</strong> Player links are:</p>
<ul><li>A) Created by CS</li><li>B) In the app store</li><li>C) Club-managed</li><li>D) Auto-generated</li></ul>
<p><strong>27.</strong> Cancellation requires verifying the order is:</p>
<ul><li>A) Personalized</li><li>B) Not yet fulfilled</li><li>C) Delivered</li><li>D) Refunded</li></ul>
<p><strong>28.</strong> Internal details belong in:</p>
<ul><li>A) The customer email</li><li>B) A separate internal note</li><li>C) The subject line</li><li>D) The tracking field</li></ul>
<p><strong>29.</strong> The one-time courtesy for "add items" is to:</p>
<ul><li>A) Give a free upgrade</li><li>B) Give a coupon</li><li>C) Refund the new order's shipping</li><li>D) Merge the orders</li></ul>
<p><strong>30.</strong> A package scanned "delivered" but not received:</p>
<ul><li>A) Auto-refund</li><li>B) Verify scan/address, consider a carrier claim, escalate</li><li>C) Ignore</li><li>D) Reship blindly</li></ul></body></html>